.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt SSH3-CA 1
.Os ssh3-c
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3-ca
.Nd the own certification authority of the ssh3-c set
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the certification authority of one installation (the wave 19,
PLAN.md 19): the root, the issuance of the server and the client
certificates from the CSRs, the revocation with the CRL, the
rotation of the root.  The state lives in one directory
.Sy SSH3_CA_DIR
or
.Pa ~/.ssh3/ca :
.Pa ca.key
(the root private key, 0600, ed25519),
.Pa ca.pem
(the self-signed root, 10 years),
.Pa index
(the flat ledger of the issuance),
.Pa crl.pem
(after the first revoke).
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Ar dir
Generate the root and the fresh state directory.  An existing
.Sy ca.key
declines - the state never overwrites silently.
.It Cm sign-server Ar csr.pem Ar out.pem
Issue the server certificate of the CSR: the SAN rides the request,
825 days, the chain (leaf + root) lands in
.Ar out.pem .
The server consumes the file directly
(-c), the clients pin it as an ordinary anchor or trust the root.
.It Cm sign-client Ar csr.pem Ar out.pem Ar user
Issue the client certificate: the CN rides
.Ar user ,
the mapping of the server auth (the phase 3 of PLAN.md 14) reads
the user from the CN and the SAN spki/email of the presented cert.
.It Cm revoke Ar serial | Ar cert.pem
Mark the certificate revoked (the serial of the issuance or the
cert file), regenerate
.Pa crl.pem .
The CRL enforcement on the server side rides the next increment -
the boundary documents PLAN.md 19.
.It Cm rotate
Back the whole state aside
.Pa ( dir.old.<epoch> )
and run init again.  The certs of the old root need a re-issuance
(the other issuer) - the tool prints the count.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy SSH3_CA_DIR
The state directory (the default ~/.ssh3/ca).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh3-cert 1 ,
.Xr ssh3-server 8 ,
.Xr ssh3 1
